    <briefdescription>
<para>Implementation for watchdog: Starts the monitoring thread that periodically checks a pooled connection. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This file implements <ref refid="classWatchDog" kindref="compound">WatchDog</ref>. The constructor guards against a pre-existing thread and then launches a lambda that loops while the atomic flag is set. Each cycle leases a connection with an RAII handler, checks it, and on failure reconnects it and asks the pool to reconnect all idle links. <ref refid="classDatabaseBusy" kindref="compound">DatabaseBusy</ref> and other exceptions are caught and followed by an interval sleep. The destructor clears the flag and joins the thread before the watchdog object disappears.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: It is the server&apos;s automatic recovery mechanism for the synchronous database path. A database restart or a dropped socket is detected here within one second and repaired without any request failing permanently. Because the monitor leases its connection through a <ref refid="classDatabaseHanndler" kindref="compound">DatabaseHanndler</ref>, it also participates in the same pool and back-pressure rules as regular requests. Without this file, stale connections would keep failing until manual intervention.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>std::thread and lambdas as thread entry points: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/thread">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/thread</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::atomic (the stop flag shared between threads): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>RAII with std::unique_ptr (automatic cleanup): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/unique_ptr">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/unique_ptr</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Exceptions and catch blocks: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/try_catch">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/try_catch</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::this_thread::sleep_for (pause a thread): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/sleep_for">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/sleep_for</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
